    win:{ expertTitle:"The Dose Chain Proven", expert:["You name <b>Dr. Halvard Bre — clinic director</b>, <b>The Clinic Director's Office</b>, and <b>A calibration & QA gap in the treatment chain</b>. Not a rogue software or computer glitch. Not a one-off patient reaction — sheer misfortune. Source change, output drift, treatment geometry, and repeated injury align quantitatively.","Your reconstruction follows the prescription through calibration and delivery, demonstrating why a systematic dose error can be repeated with perfect software obedience."], soundTitle:"A Defensible Physics Finding", sound:["You correctly connect <b>Dr. Halvard Bre — clinic director</b>, <b>The Clinic Director's Office</b>, and <b>A calibration & QA gap in the treatment chain</b>. The absorbed-dose case is strong, though one independent detector result receives limited explanation.","The clinic commission accepts the conclusion because patient patterns and machine measurements agree across separate evidentiary paths."], namedTitle:"The Dose Error Named", named:["You select <b>Dr. Halvard Bre — clinic director</b>, <b>The Clinic Director's Office</b>, and <b>A calibration & QA gap in the treatment chain</b>, while leaving the transition from machine output to tissue dose mostly asserted.","The accusation survives, but physicists must still rebuild the calibration chain before any beam can return to treatment."] },
    overclaim:{ title:"Software Becomes a Phantom Culprit", body:["You choose <b>A rogue software or computer glitch</b>, even though the code executed a beam model fed by unchecked physical output. A computer label cannot account for measured excess dose.","The sensational theory obscures <b>A calibration & QA gap in the treatment chain</b>, the narrower finding that can be demonstrated with phantoms, detector readings, and patient geometry."] },
    dismissal:{ title:"Injury Dismissed as Biology", body:["You accept <b>A one-off patient reaction — sheer misfortune</b>, ignoring the recurrence of similar damage after the same machine change and missing physics checks.","Treating each burn as personal sensitivity leaves a systematic calibration failure available to injure the next scheduled patient."] },
